Revision history for SICK-Target-CiscoSB

{{$NEXT}}
    - Initial release
    - SICK::Target::CiscoSB: device type "cisco-sb" for SICK - certificates
      for the web interface of Cisco Small Business switches (Sx300, SG300,
      SG500); imports certificate and key (mode "import", the default) or
      has the switch write a certificate request for its own key (mode
      "csr"), makes the slot the active one and saves the configuration;
      never sends an import the switch would answer by deleting the key of
      the slot (a certificate that does not belong to the key)
    - SICK::Target::CiscoSB::Session: the command line dialog - login at the
      prompts of the switch, prompts with log lines behind them, redrawn
      and scrolled lines, (Y/N) questions, paging, time limits that say
      what was waited for
    - SICK::Target::CiscoSB::Transport::SSH: the connection through the ssh
      program of the system, old key exchange and host key algorithms on
      request, host key checking always on - a host key that ssh cannot
      store (a known hosts file that cannot be written) ends the connection
      instead of being accepted unchecked every time
    - SICK::Target::CiscoSB::Transport::Replay: recorded dialogs in place of
      a switch, for tests
    - docs/device-notes.md: what an SG300-20 with firmware 1.4.11.5 does,
      dialog by dialog
    - SICK::Target::CiscoSB, its Session and both transports are Moo classes;
      the transports share the role SICK::Target::CiscoSB::Transport, which
      the session requires, and the target checks key against certificate with
      SICK::Bundle's key_matches (needs the SICK core at or after its
      key_matches change). Depends on Moo, namespace::autoclean, Type::Tiny
      and Path::Tiny.
